{"kind":"FETCH","data":{"headers":{},"body":"{\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"fca84a0a-46ff-482c-9523-18394f13f136\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Compulsory acquisition under Article 300A must ordinarily serve which purpose?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 300A के अधीन अनिवार्य अर्जन को सामान्यतः किस प्रयोजन की पूर्ति करनी चाहिए?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"A purely personal favour\",\"hi\":\"पूर्णतः निजी उपकार\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"A public purpose\",\"hi\":\"लोक प्रयोजन\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"An undisclosed partisan goal\",\"hi\":\"अप्रकट दलीय लक्ष्य\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No identifiable purpose\",\"hi\":\"कोई पहचान योग्य प्रयोजन नहीं\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=45 — 2025 judgment, paragraph 41 quoting Kolkata Municipal Corporation, PDF page 45: notice, hearing, reasoned decision, public purpose and fair compensation\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"State of Himachal Pradesh v. Rajesh Chander Sood\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=45\",\"citation\":\"2025 judgment, paragraph 41 quoting Kolkata Municipal Corporation, PDF page 45: notice, hearing, reasoned decision, public purpose and fair compensation\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Rajesh Chander Sood judgment, paragraph 41, official PDF page 45\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f8e70ef7-d4be-4d80-8976-87fc4ab66c0f\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 300A is located in which Part of the Constitution?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 300A संविधान के किस भाग में स्थित है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Part XII\",\"hi\":\"भाग XII\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Part III\",\"hi\":\"भाग III\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Part IV\",\"hi\":\"भाग IV\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Part IVA\",\"hi\":\"भाग IVA\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf#page=201 — Part XII, Chapter IV, Article 300A and Forty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 201 (document page 170)\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2026)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/88cca69e868e50b217f855be2fb8bdba.pdf#page=201\",\"citation\":\"Part XII, Chapter IV, Article 300A and Forty-fourth Amendment footnote, PDF page 201 (document page 170)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 300A and insertion footnote, official PDF page 201\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f75c71c3-79ea-441c-b75c-468b4c26ad3a\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Which personal interest has been recognised under Article 21 alongside privacy and dignity?\",\"hi\":\"निजता और गरिमा के साथ किस व्यक्तिगत हित को अनुच्छेद 21 के अधीन मान्यता मिली है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Reputation\",\"hi\":\"प्रतिष्ठा\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Hereditary title\",\"hi\":\"वंशानुगत उपाधि\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Tax immunity\",\"hi\":\"कर उन्मुक्ति\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"A right to defame others\",\"hi\":\"दूसरों को बदनाम करने का अधिकार\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=428 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 65 footnote, PDF page 428: judicially recognised Article 21 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=428\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 65 footnote, PDF page 428: judicially recognised Article 21 protections\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraph 65 footnote, official PDF page 428\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f7271adc-c608-472c-aad2-7aeaba21262d\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 21A expressly covers children in which age group?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21A स्पष्टतः किस आयु-वर्ग के बच्चों को आच्छादित करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Three to six years\",\"hi\":\"तीन से छह वर्ष\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Six to fourteen years\",\"hi\":\"छह से चौदह वर्ष\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Fourteen to eighteen years\",\"hi\":\"चौदह से अठारह वर्ष\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Eighteen to twenty-one years\",\"hi\":\"अठारह से इक्कीस वर्ष\"}},\"difficulty\":\"basic\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42 — Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6 — Printed page 31, PDF page 6: Right to Freedom overview and Articles 19-22 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=6\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 31, PDF page 6: Right to Freedom overview and Articles 19-22 protections\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), official PDF page 42; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 31\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"RAILWAY\",\"STATE_ONEDAY\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"f5bedb28-c6c7-4457-9bc5-fb2ddcc861cc\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A visitor who is not an Indian citizen asks whether the beneficiary wording of Articles 19 and 21 is identical. Which answer follows from the text?\",\"hi\":\"एक ऐसा आगंतुक जो भारतीय नागरिक नहीं है पूछता है कि क्या अनुच्छेद 19 और 21 की लाभार्थी-भाषा समान है। पाठ से कौन-सा उत्तर निकलता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"No; Article 19 is framed for citizens, while Article 21 protects any person\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; अनुच्छेद 19 नागरिकों के लिए है, जबकि अनुच्छेद 21 किसी भी व्यक्ति की रक्षा करता है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"Yes; both apply only to citizens by birth\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; दोनों केवल जन्मजात नागरिकों पर लागू होते हैं\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Yes; both protect only elected representatives\",\"hi\":\"हाँ; दोनों केवल निर्वाचित प्रतिनिधियों की रक्षा करते हैं\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"No; Article 19 protects only non-citizens\",\"hi\":\"नहीं; अनुच्छेद 19 केवल गैर-नागरिकों की रक्षा करता है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40 — Part III, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), PDF page 40 (document page 9); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42 — Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=9 — Printed page 34, PDF page 9: meaning of liberty, Article 21 and arrest safeguards\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=40\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), PDF page 40 (document page 9)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=42\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), PDF page 42 (document page 11)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=9\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 34, PDF page 9: meaning of liberty, Article 21 and arrest safeguards\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 19(1)(a)-(d), official PDF page 40; Constitution of India, Articles 19(6), 20, 21, 21A and 22(1), official PDF page 42; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 34\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ef9fa1a2-8c65-4ad9-a734-3ac37cb99bf1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"A municipality removes the only means by which a group earns its livelihood, without lawful authority or a fair procedure. Which Article 21 principle is most relevant?\",\"hi\":\"नगरपालिका किसी समूह के जीवन-निर्वाह के एकमात्र साधन को बिना विधिक प्राधिकार या न्यायसंगत प्रक्रिया के हटा देती है। अनुच्छेद 21 का कौन-सा सिद्धांत सर्वाधिक प्रासंगिक है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Every occupation is unregulatable\",\"hi\":\"प्रत्येक व्यवसाय अविनियमनीय है\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The group owns all public land\",\"hi\":\"समूह समस्त सार्वजनिक भूमि का स्वामी है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Livelihood is an incident of life, so deprivation requires lawful and fair treatment\",\"hi\":\"आजीविका जीवन का आनुषंगिक अंग है, अतः वंचन विधिसम्मत और न्यायसंगत होना चाहिए\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Article 21 concerns elections only\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 21 केवल चुनावों से संबंधित है\"}},\"difficulty\":\"advanced\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=110 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraphs 113-114, PDF page 110: dignified existence and livelihood as an incident of life; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=210 — Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 150, PDF page 210: fair and reasonable procedure and Article 21 protections\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=110\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraphs 113-114, PDF page 110: dignified existence and livelihood as an incident of life\"},{\"title\":\"Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd.) v. Union of India\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2012/35071/35071_2012_Judgement_24-Aug-2017.pdf#page=210\",\"citation\":\"Nine-Judge Bench judgment dated 24 August 2017, paragraph 150, PDF page 210: fair and reasonable procedure and Article 21 protections\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[],\"evidence_locator\":\"K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraphs 113-114, official PDF page 110; K.S. Puttaswamy judgment, paragraph 150, official PDF page 210\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"ed7c4df8-d919-4111-a443-29d9607741a1\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"Article 22(3) excludes which two categories from clauses (1) and (2)?\",\"hi\":\"अनुच्छेद 22(3) किन दो श्रेणियों को खंड (1) और (2) से बाहर रखता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Enemy aliens and persons arrested or detained under preventive-detention law\",\"hi\":\"शत्रु अन्यदेशीय और निवारक-निरोध विधि के अधीन गिरफ्तार या निरुद्ध व्यक्ति\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"All citizens and all children\",\"hi\":\"सभी नागरिक और सभी बच्चे\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Only convicted prisoners and witnesses\",\"hi\":\"केवल दोषसिद्ध बंदी और साक्षी\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Legislators and judges\",\"hi\":\"विधायक और न्यायाधीश\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=43 — Part III, Article 22(2)-(4) and current-text footnote, PDF page 43 (document page 12); Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India — https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=44 — Part III, Article 22(4)-(7), PDF page 44 (document page 13); National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT) — https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=10 — Printed page 35, PDF page 10: preventive detention and reasonable restrictions\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=43\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 22(2)-(4) and current-text footnote, PDF page 43 (document page 12)\"},{\"title\":\"The Constitution of India (official Hindi-English diglot edition, as on 1 May 2024)\",\"institution\":\"Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India\",\"url\":\"https://www.legislative.gov.in/static/uploads/2025/07/ca7ce5c746fa7480804bbdeb6cb704f0.pdf#page=44\",\"citation\":\"Part III, Article 22(4)-(7), PDF page 44 (document page 13)\"}],\"secondary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"Indian Constitution at Work, Class XI, Chapter 2: Rights in the Indian Constitution (Reprint 2026-27)\",\"institution\":\"National Council of Educational Research and Training (NCERT)\",\"url\":\"https://ncert.nic.in/textbook/pdf/keps202.pdf#page=10\",\"citation\":\"Printed page 35, PDF page 10: preventive detention and reasonable restrictions\"}],\"evidence_locator\":\"Constitution of India, Article 22(2)-(4), official PDF page 43; Constitution of India, Article 22(4)-(7), official PDF page 44; NCERT Class XI, Indian Constitution at Work, Chapter 2, printed page 35\"},\"year\":null,\"pyq_exam_name\":null,\"exam_tags\":[\"SSC\",\"STATE_PCS\",\"UPSC\"],\"attempt_count\":0,\"correct_count\":0},{\"id\":\"eb2865fb-a825-49fa-b07d-da036eb4f4d4\",\"question_text\":{\"en\":\"What does the right to an efficient and expeditious acquisition process require?\",\"hi\":\"दक्ष और शीघ्र अर्जन-प्रक्रिया का अधिकार क्या अपेक्षा करता है?\"},\"options\":{\"A\":{\"en\":\"Proceedings should follow prescribed timelines without avoidable delay\",\"hi\":\"कार्यवाही निर्धारित समय-सीमाओं के अनुसार अनावश्यक विलंब के बिना चले\"},\"B\":{\"en\":\"The State may keep proceedings pending forever\",\"hi\":\"राज्य कार्यवाही अनिश्चितकाल लंबित रख सकता है\"},\"C\":{\"en\":\"Notice may always be skipped\",\"hi\":\"सूचना सदैव छोड़ी जा सकती है\"},\"D\":{\"en\":\"Compensation may never be determined\",\"hi\":\"प्रतिकर कभी निर्धारित न किया जाए\"}},\"difficulty\":\"intermediate\",\"source\":\"QuestionWale Original | Verified v2026-07-18: Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=46 — 2025 judgment, paragraphs 41, 43-45, PDF page 46: expeditious process, conclusion, fair compensation and corresponding State duties; Supreme Court of India — https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=47 — 2025 judgment, paragraphs 46-48, PDF page 47: constitutional/human right, rehabilitation and timely payment of compensation\",\"source_metadata\":{\"primary_sources\":[{\"title\":\"State of Himachal Pradesh v. Rajesh Chander Sood\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=46\",\"citation\":\"2025 judgment, paragraphs 41, 43-45, PDF page 46: expeditious process, conclusion, fair compensation and corresponding State duties\"},{\"title\":\"State of Himachal Pradesh v. Rajesh Chander Sood\",\"institution\":\"Supreme Court of India\",\"url\":\"https://api.sci.gov.in/supremecourt/2023/14014/14014_2023_2_1501_58185_Judgement_02-Jan-2025.pdf#page=47\",\"citation\":\"2025 judgment, paragraphs 46-48, PDF page 47: constitutional/human right, rehabilitation and time